      "query": "How long must a password be when used as the only authentication factor?",
      "dense": [
        {
          "id": "nist-sp800-63b-4::chunk-114",
          "content": "choose a different password. Other composition requirements for passwords SHALL NOT\nbe imposed. A rationale for this is presented in Appendix A, Strength of Passwords.\n3.1.1.2. Password Verifiers\nThe following requirements apply to passwords.\n1. Verifiers and CSPs SHALL require passwords that are used as a single-factor\nauthentication mechanism to be a minimum of 15 characters in length. Verifiers\nand CSPs MAY allow passwords that are only used as part of multi-factor",
          "metadata": {
