          "id": "nist-sp800-63b-4::chunk-242",
          "content": "3.2.5. Phishing Resistance\nPhishing attacks, previously referred to in SP 800-63B as “verifier impersonation,” are\nattempts by fraudulent verifiers and RPs to fool an unwary claimant into presenting an\nauthenticator to an impostor. In some prior versions of SP 800-63, protocols that are\nresistant to phishing attacks were also referred to as “strongly MitM-resistant.”\nIn this document, phishing resistance is the ability of the authentication protocol to",
